    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1503" root="اول" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِيلَةٌ</span></b>  sometimes signifies The <i>relations to whom
one goes</i> [or <i>is traced</i>] <i>back in genealogy.</i> (Ibn-
'Abbád.) [See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آلٌ</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  You say also, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَدَدْتُهُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِلَى إِيلَتِهِ</span> <i>I made him to go back,</i> or <i>revert, to
his natural disposition:</i> or, <i>to his</i> [<i>original</i>] <i>state</i>
or <i>condition.</i> (Ibn-'Abbád.)

